The current representation of REST resources of time-series data (e.g. aggregate counter) can lead to problems in consuming applications. 
Despite the time series data provided by the "counts" data structure is logically ordered by key (timestamps) it doesn't guarantee an ordering, since many consuming applications interpret JSON data as an unordered map like data structure. Because of this consuming applications have to apply special ordering / transformation logic in order to get the data in an chronologically ordered fashion. It would be helpful if one could configure the rendering of the time series data, e.g. as a list of json object like:
{code:json}
{
 "ts":"Sun Oct 12 23:10:23 CEST 2014"
 ,"value": 42
} 
{code}
Where {ts} denotes the timestamp and {value} denotes the value.

